retries when the server returns 503. It makes at most 3 attempts and waits longer between each one. I checked it against a local HTTP server and it behaves as intended.\n\n**The change, in `weather.py`:**\n- A 503 makes `urllib` raise `HTTPError`. `get` catches it, waits `backoff * 2**attempt` seconds (0.5s, then 1s by default), and tries again.\n- Any other HTTP error is raised straight away. A 503 on the last attempt is raised as normal.\n- Two new optional constructor arguments, `max_attempts=3` and `backoff=0.5`. Existing calls don't need to change.\n\n**Test runs:**\n\n| Server behaviour | Requests made | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| 503 twice, then 200 | 3 | Returned the JSON |\n| Always 503 | 3 | Raised the 503 |\n| 500 | 1 | Raised right away, no retry |\n\n**Limits:**\n- Timeouts and connection errors are not retried; only a 503 triggers a retry.\n- The `Retry-After` header is ignored, so the wait is always the fixed schedule above.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 35428, "requests_cache_write": 177240, "requests_cost_usd": 0.9281216000000001, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1739, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial3", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 4, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:36:23.946809+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 22.998, "t_checker_s": 2.382, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 360, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1753, "tokens_cache_read": 35428, "tokens_cache_write": 177240, "to